      "mistakes": [
        {
          "wrong": "저는 못 수영해요",
          "right": "저는 수영 못 해요",
          "why_uz": "N하다 fe'llarida 못 ot bilan 하다 orasiga kiradi.",
          "why_en": "In N하다 verbs, 못 goes between the noun and 하다."
        },
        {
          "wrong": "날씨가 못 좋아요",
          "right": "날씨가 안 좋아요",
          "why_uz": "Sifat bilan 못 emas, 안 ishlatiladi.",
          "why_en": "With an adjective, use 안, not 못."
        },
        {
          "wrong": "고기를 못 먹어요 (xohlamaganda)",
          "right": "고기를 안 먹어요",
          "why_uz": "O'z tanlovingiz bo'lsa — 안. Qo'lingizdan kelmasa — 못.",
          "why_en": "If it's your own choice — 안. If you're not able to — 못."
        }
      ],
      "uz_compare": "O'zbekchada ikki xil inkor bor: 'yemayman' (안 먹어요) va 'yeya olmayman' (못 먹어요). Koreyschada ham xuddi shunday: 안 — xohlamaslik, 못 — qila olmaslik.",
      "compare_en": "English has the same two negatives: 'I don't eat' (안 먹어요) and 'I can't eat' (못 먹어요). Korean works the same way: 안 — not wanting to, 못 — not being able to."
