      "meaning_uz": "Xohish: '...-moqchiman', '...-gim keladi'",
      "meaning_en": "Want: 'I want to…'",
      "explanation_md": "**-고 싶다** fe'lga qo'shilib, **xohish**ni bildiradi: o'zbekchadagi **\"-moqchiman / -gim keladi\"**.\n\n**테니스를 배우고 싶어요.** — *Tennisni o'rganmoqchiman.*\n\n### Qanday yasaladi\n\nO'zakka **-고 싶어요** qo'shiladi, 받침ga qarab o'zgarmaydi:\n\n- 배우다 → **배우고 싶어요**\n- 먹다 → **먹고 싶어요**\n- 쉬다 → **쉬고 싶어요**\n\nO'tgan zamon: **-고 싶었어요** (xohlagan edim). Inkor: **안 -고 싶어요** yoki **-고 싶지 않아요** (3-bo'limdagi -지 않다!).\n\n### Kim xohlaydi?\n\n- **Men** va savolda **siz**: **-고 싶어요** — 뭐 먹**고 싶어요**? (Nima yemoqchisiz?)\n- **Boshqa odam (u)**: **-고 싶어해요** — 동생은 축구를 하**고 싶어해요**. (Ukam futbol o'ynamoqchi.)\n\nKoreyschada boshqa odamning ichki xohishini to'g'ridan-to'g'ri aytish g'alati eshitiladi, shuning uchun 3-shaxsda **-어하다** qo'shiladi.",
      "explanation_md_en": "**-고 싶다** is added to a verb to show a **wish**: English **\"want to…\"**.\n\n**테니스를 배우고 싶어요.** — *I want to learn tennis.*\n\n### How to form it\n\nAdd **-고 싶어요** to the stem; it doesn't change with 받침:\n\n- 배우다 → **배우고 싶어요**\n- 먹다 → **먹고 싶어요**\n- 쉬다 → **쉬고 싶어요**\n\nPast: **-고 싶었어요** (I wanted to). Negative: **안 -고 싶어요** or **-고 싶지 않아요** (the -지 않다 from Unit 3!).\n\n### Who wants?\n\n- **I**, and **you** in questions: **-고 싶어요** — 뭐 먹**고 싶어요**? (What do you want to eat?)\n- **Someone else (he/she)**: **-고 싶어해요** — 동생은 축구를 하**고 싶어해요**. (My brother wants to play football.)\n\nIn Korean it sounds odd to state another person's inner wish directly, so for the third person **-어하다** is added.",
      "formation": [
        {
          "condition_uz": "Men / siz (savol)",
          "condition_en": "I / you (question)",
          "rule": "-고 싶어요",
          "example": "배우다 → 배우고 싶어요"
        },
        {
          "condition_uz": "O'tgan zamon",
          "condition_en": "Past tense",
          "rule": "-고 싶었어요",
          "example": "가다 → 가고 싶었어요"
        },
        {
          "condition_uz": "3-shaxs (u)",
          "condition_en": "Third person (he / she)",
          "rule": "-고 싶어해요",
          "example": "하다 → 하고 싶어해요"
        }
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "ko": "테니스를 배우고 싶어요.",
